{"id": "EUVD-2026-45650", "enisaUuid": "11a77bbb-7ef5-3b75-bd15-b4e11f90998b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: ebtables: move to two-stage removal scheme\n\nLike previous patches for x_tables, follow same pattern in ebtables.\nWe can't reuse xt helpers: ebt_table struct layout is incompatible.\n\ntable->ops assignment is now done while still holding the ebt mutex\nto make sure we never expose partially-filled table struct.", "datePublished": "2026-07-19T15:39:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:02", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6fe4c808b6cdb405ed64ea6e740d557bba3d7745", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f34e5a674afe743d1af80684d64b511f40a5c35d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/739d5dac7b2da44a756aa4d758ee3f1ccf5a27f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef395579a7631a06d61969fc712eb80402231b89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7f0544d86d439cb946515d2ef6a0a75e8626710"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2pwc-rv94-9pp5", "CVE-2026-64077"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00fdaf6a-0941-3a17-b114-2ea2da749417", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "050a8611-4df8-32eb-8ec5-20a24335da5a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "87663c39f898b18905499126548da61450628682 <739d5dac7b2da44a756aa4d758ee3f1ccf5a27f1"}, {"id": "231ccd6b-96ff-3109-92c2-10ba39c9922a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "87663c39f898b18905499126548da61450628682 <b7f0544d86d439cb946515d2ef6a0a75e8626710"}, {"id": "33aaa0af-0ea6-383f-885e-8cbf38202600", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "87663c39f898b18905499126548da61450628682 <6fe4c808b6cdb405ed64ea6e740d557bba3d7745"}, {"id": "4da59cad-18af-3b05-b14d-947